From: SamuriHL <samurihl@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Nov 2026 12:10:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] bdj: an Ixc call into a callee destroyed during the call fails fast

A remote call whose callee xlet is destroyed while the call runs never
answers: the caller joins its remote thread with no bound, so the
caller's own destroyXlet (and with it BDJAppProxy.release()) waits for
the 5 s STOP timeout and the Ixc thread's 1 s wait before the shutdown
goes on. On Universal discs (M3GAN 2.0, UniversalTitleBoundXlet calling
TitleChangeHandler.titleDestroyed() on the title xlet it is stopping
with) every disc stop and every Kodi quit with the menu up paid about
6.5 s for it.

The caller now joins in 100 ms steps and, when the callee's context is
released or its xlet is DESTROYED, interrupts the remote thread and
throws RemoteException("callee destroyed during remote execution"), as
invoke() already refuses a call into a released callee. Logged at ERROR
("invoke(): callee destroyed during remote execution, call abandoned")
so a gate can count it.

---
--- a/src/libbluray/bdj/java/org/videolan/IxcRegistryImpl.java
+++ b/src/libbluray/bdj/java/org/videolan/IxcRegistryImpl.java
@@ -39,6 +39,8 @@
 
 import javax.tv.xlet.XletContext;
 
+import org.dvb.application.AppProxy;
+
 import org.videolan.BDJXletContext;
 
 
@@ -208,6 +210,14 @@
             this.remoteObj = remoteObj;
         }
 
+        private boolean calleeGone(BDJXletContext context) {
+            if (null == context || context.isReleased()) {
+                return true;
+            }
+            AppProxy proxy = context.getAppProxy();
+            return proxy != null && proxy.getState() == AppProxy.DESTROYED;
+        }
+
         public Object invoke(Object proxy, Method method, Object[] args) throws Throwable {
             if (null == remoteObj.context || remoteObj.context.isReleased()) {
                 Debug("invoke(): callee has been destroyed");
@@ -237,7 +247,22 @@
             remoteMethod.callerContext.addIxcThread(remoteThread);
             remoteThread.setDaemon(false);
             remoteThread.start();
-            remoteThread.join();
+            /* A callee destroyed during the call (its xlet stopped, or its context released) never
+             * answers: fail as a call into a destroyed callee does above, instead of holding the
+             * caller (and its xlet's stop) until the caller is killed. */
+            while (true) {
+                remoteThread.join(100);
+                if (!remoteThread.isAlive()) {
+                    break;
+                }
+                if (calleeGone(remoteObj.context)) {
+                    logger.error("invoke(): callee destroyed during remote execution, call abandoned: " +
+                                 method + " (callee " + remoteObj.context + ")");
+                    remoteThread.interrupt();
+                    remoteMethod.callerContext.removeIxcThread(remoteThread);
+                    throw new RemoteException("callee destroyed during remote execution");
+                }
+            }
             remoteMethod.callerContext.removeIxcThread(remoteThread);
 
             if (!remoteMethod.finished) {
